    "created_at": "2026-10-01T21:54:40Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-10-01T21:54:40Z",
    "body": "Current Chromium makes this example especially relevant for latency-sensitive applications.\n\n`USBDevice` is exposed in Dedicated Workers, and opening a device registers `kWebUSB` with `DisableAggressiveThrottling()`. That gives the spec example a useful concrete architecture: perform `requestDevice()` in the Window, recover the permitted device with `getDevices()` in the worker, then keep the transfer loop off the main event loop.\n\nIt would also be worth showing how to disambiguate the selected device without relying on array index, since that problem has already come up in this thread.\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
